Instrumented CPU driver SHA-256: 5ffda2f1fc01c5d5ff5513715918e56a8302f8137cb2b3f0250db699c825c19f.
CUDA drivers and scoped SDK are the unchanged hash-bound artifacts in iqa_cuda_deployment_2026-10-12.meta, GPU source ec453ab069. Runner/worker/controller/ledger-reader are unchanged from iqa_deployment_dct_2026-10-12.meta; deployed zenbench remains ac675d3a, version 0.1.10, not the pending 0.1.11 release.
Direct controls: all 38 SDR routes at 1024x1024 patterned sRGB8; hdrvdp/hdrvdp3 at 1024x768 absolute BT.709 nits; all six CUDA variants at 1024x1024, cold and warm_instance. Two score operations, packed and padded inputs, separate ordinary and instrumented processes. Expected products are exact per host, route and workload; these controls do not compare CPU to GPU or one host to another.
Inventory command: python3 -B scripts/jobsys/build_benchmark_study.py inventory. The source inventory contains 46 variants; every one has a native driver route. GPU cold/warm-instance modes add six repeated routes, yielding 52 ordinary latency and 52 separate memory observations per host. Native worker collection requires every packet status complete, not merely ledger Done.
CPU campaign: just iqa-deployment-campaign <binaries> <runner> <checker-tree> <new-root>/cpu <machine> <domain> --sdr-size 1024 1024 --hdr-size 1024 768.
GPU controls: CUDA_PATH=<sdk> LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<sdk>/lib64 just iqa-gpu-check <GPU-binaries> cuda <new-root>/gpu-controls <adapter-resolved-with-nvidia-smi> --size 1024 1024.
GPU worker: just iqa-gpu-deployment-bench <GPU-binaries> <runner> <new-root>/gpu-controls <new-root>/gpu <machine> <domain> <sdk>.
Portable checkers: just iqa-control-tree <new-archive>; extract under checker-tree. An initial i134 transfer omitted the registry and failed before any controls ran. Its log and empty campaign root remain at ~/tmp/zm-iqa-expanded-20261012/campaign-first-failure.log and cpu-first-failure; the completed source-tree recipe was used for both successful launches.
Resource boundary: outer systemd system service, normal User, AllowedCPUs=2, MemoryMax=17179869184, MemorySwapMax=0, properties verified while active. Worker reports one CPU core, so jobs run serially. Inner run-heavy reports no user scope and is niced/monitored; the outer unit supplies the hard limits. Its peak RSS receipt differs from per-case resident/heap memory, and from the unit's total charged memory including filesystem cache.
i134 complete raw paths: ~/tmp/zm-iqa-expanded-20261012/cpu/{sdr-controls,hdr-controls,benchmark-observations}, gpu-controls, gpu, campaign.log. Domain performance_l320480K. SDK and GPU binaries remain under ~/tmp/zm-iqa-cuda-20261012/.
